<title>EGYPT: Egypt welcomes IBCA investment grade rating.</title>
<headline>Egypt welcomes IBCA investment grade rating.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian Economy Minister Youssef Boutros Ghali said on Tuesday that he welcomed European credit rating agency IBCA's investment grade rating for Egypt.</p>
<p>&quot;It will assure investors of the worthiness of investing in Egypt and of its stability,&quot; the minister said in a statement sent to Reuters.</p>
<p>He said that the assessment was especially relevant because it means Egypt no longer had a split rating, between Moody's below investment grade rating and Standard and Poor's investment grade.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +2 02 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
